# A record on a reference place to an ordinary Structure launches it (R22, item 2; plan M11 5b): `p: other` runs Model
# over the data other, and the unknown name other answers 3, as the receiver call answers with such data (R22, item 3).
# Formerly the form was refused (8, slice 346); a reference to an int is declare_place_reference.
# Plan M11 5v: the declarations of ordinary Structures live in the data part of main; the reference place p stays at the
# root and points into that data by path (a reference declaration in a data part is not executed yet).
# The code of main is a bare `return`: a method with one parenthesized part and no code reads that part as its code,
# and then main() itself answers 3, before the record `p: other` is reached.
sub: main () (
    Model:
        int: v 1
)
    return
main()
@: p main\data\Model
p: other
int: after main\data\Model\v
